# First of two runs sharing one --nvram file (tests/CMakeLists.txt): an empty
# battery-backed RAM stops POST at its NVR line, and Reset repairs and writes
# the setup, then goes to the start-up screen (no key is held at power-on, so
# not to Offline Setup; the keys below change nothing there). The second run
# checks that the written setup survives.
policy log
speed max
run #300000000
key lctrl
run #400000000
# the first key after boot is swallowed
key down
run #5000000
key rctrl
run #60000000
key down
run #5000000
key space
run #20000000
key f3
run #30000000
key f3
run #100000000
quit
